{%- comment -%}
  ZOREV — cinematic hero.

  A full-bleed place, not a product on paper: the first screen should say
  where these things are carried before it says what they are. The copy sits
  in the quiet side of the frame; the products are one step below (#line),
  and on a wide screen a small printed card in the corner names them, so a
  first-time visitor never has to guess what the shop sells.

  V15 motion, all transform-only and all in CSS (zorev-film.css):
    1  breathe   the photograph drifts in scale (1.02 -> 1.07) over 40 s,
                 eased and alternating, around the image's focal point, so
                 there is no loop point to notice
    2  depth     as the hero scrolls away the photograph lags the page by a
                 few percent: a CSS scroll-driven animation, so it costs no
                 script, and browsers without scroll timelines keep it still
    3  light     drawn light shafts and mist, OFF by default ("Drawn light
                 and mist"): the photograph already has real fog and light
  The copy is visible from the first paint; it only settles a few pixels as
  the page opens (transform, never opacity), so it never delays the LCP.
  Under prefers-reduced-motion everything is a still photograph. The veil
  keeps the copy at AA contrast over the photograph (measured on phones:
  the eyebrow is the weakest line, >= 5.4:1 at the 5th percentile).

  A film (Shopify-hosted, silent, looping) plays over the photograph while
  on screen, with a pause button, never under reduced motion or Save-Data.
  Empty photograph and film: the section falls back to the dark band with
  the copy, so it never renders as a broken frame.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings
  assign pa = s.product_a | default: settings.pair_product_a
  assign pb = s.product_b | default: settings.pair_product_b
  assign has_media = false
  if s.photo != blank or s.video != blank
    assign has_media = true
  endif
  assign show_card = false
  if s.show_card and pa != blank and pa.title != blank and pb != blank and pb.title != blank
    assign show_card = true
  endif
  assign from = pa.price
  if pb.price < from
    assign from = pb.price
  endif

  comment
    The breathe scales around the photograph's focal point (Content >
    Files), so the subject stays put while the frame drifts. An unset focal
    point reads 50/50; the trail photograph's light then gets the old
    hand-set origin.
  endcomment
  assign fx = '58%'
  assign fy = '46%'
  assign fp = s.photo.presentation.focal_point
  if s.photo != blank and fp != blank
    unless fp.x == 50 and fp.y == 50
      assign fx = fp.x | append: '%'
      assign fy = fp.y | append: '%'
    endunless
  endif
  assign fxm = '50%'
  assign fym = '50%'
  assign fpm = s.photo_mobile.presentation.focal_point
  if s.photo_mobile != blank and fpm != blank
    assign fxm = fpm.x | append: '%'
    assign fym = fpm.y | append: '%'
  endif
-%}
{%- capture pp -%}{% render 'pair-price' %}{%- endcapture -%}
<section class="zhf zv-dark{% unless has_media %} zhf--flat{% endunless %}{% if s.drawn_light %} zhf--drawn{% endif %}" id="zhf-{{ section.id }}" data-zv-rest aria-labelledby="zhf-h-{{ section.id }}"
         style="--zhf-rays-x: {{ s.rays_x | default: 62 }}%; --zhf-rays-x-m: {{ s.rays_x_mobile | default: 34 }}%; --zhf-fx: {{ fx }}; --zhf-fy: {{ fy }}; --zhf-fx-m: {{ fxm }}; --zhf-fy-m: {{ fym }};">
  {%- if has_media -%}
    <div class="zhf__scene">
      <div class="zhf__plate">
        <div class="zhf__breathe">
          {%- comment -%}
            sizes describe the picture, not the frame: the plate is 18% taller
            than the hero and breathes up to 1.07, so on a wide screen the
            photograph is drawn about 1.25 x the viewport width, and the
            portrait phone photograph about 1.4 x (images.md §5).
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {% render 'zv-media', media: s.video, image: s.photo, image_mobile: s.photo_mobile, sizes: '125vw', sizes_mobile: '140vw', alt: s.photo_alt, eager: true, position: '50% 50%' %}
        </div>
      </div>
      {%- if s.drawn_light -%}
        <div class="zhf__rays" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="zhf__mist zhf__mist--far" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      {%- endif -%}
      <div class="zhf__veil" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="zv-wrap zhf__in">
    <div class="zhf__copy">
      {%- if s.eyebrow != blank -%}<span class="zv-eyebrow zhf__eyebrow">{{ s.eyebrow | escape }}</span>{%- endif -%}
      <h1 class="zhf__h1" id="zhf-h-{{ section.id }}">{{ s.heading | default: shop.name }}</h1>
      {%- if s.body != blank -%}<div class="zv-lead zhf__body">{{ s.body }}</div>{%- endif -%}
      {%- if s.cta_label != blank or s.cta2_label != blank -%}
        <div class="zhf__cta">
          {%- if s.cta_label != blank -%}
            <a class="zv-btn zhf__cta1" href="{{ s.cta_link | default: routes.all_products_collection_url }}">{{ s.cta_label | escape }}</a>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if s.cta2_label != blank -%}{%- unless pp == blank and s.cta2_label contains '[pair_price]' -%}
            <a class="zv-btn zv-btn--ghost zhf__cta2" href="{{ s.cta2_link | default: routes.all_products_collection_url }}">{{ s.cta2_label | replace: '[pair_price]', pp | escape }}</a>
          {%- endunless -%}{%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if s.note != blank -%}<p class="zhf__note">{{ s.note | escape }}</p>{%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- if show_card -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Printed card, not a composite: the two studio packshots sit on a
        plate of their own, so they are never pasted into the photograph's
        light. HOYGI shows its second studio image (the stick with its box,
        cut out), which stands on the plate the way GODA's packshot does.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign va = pa.selected_or_first_available_variant
        assign vb = pb.selected_or_first_available_variant
        assign ib = s.card_index_b | default: 2 | minus: 1
      -%}
      <a class="zhf__card" href="{{ s.card_link | default: '#line' }}">
        <span class="zhf__thumbs" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="zhf__thumb zv-studio">{% render 'studio-image', product: pa, variant: va, index: 0, widths: '120,180', sizes: '54px', class: 'zhf__thumb-img', loading: 'lazy', fetchpriority: 'auto', alt: '' %}</span>
          <span class="zhf__thumb zv-studio">{% render 'studio-image', product: pb, variant: vb, index: ib, widths: '120,180', sizes: '54px', class: 'zhf__thumb-img', loading: 'lazy', fetchpriority: 'auto', alt: '' %}</span>
        </span>
        <span class="zhf__card-t">
          <span class="zhf__card-k">The line</span>
          <span class="zhf__card-n">{{ pa.vendor | upcase | escape }} <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> {{ pb.vendor | upcase | escape }}</span>
          <span class="zhf__card-p">{{ pa.type | escape }} and {{ pb.type | downcase | escape }}, from {{ from | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span>
        </span>
      </a>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Cinematic hero",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "A full-width place with the copy set into its quiet side. The photograph breathes slowly and lags a little as the page scrolls; both are off for visitors who ask for reduced motion." },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "photo", "label": "Photograph", "info": "Wide 16:9, at least 2400 px across, with a dark or quiet left third for the copy (brief H1). This is the page's largest image and loads first. Set its focal point in Content > Files: the slow zoom centres on it." },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "photo_mobile", "label": "Photograph for phones", "info": "Portrait 9:16, at least 1080 × 1920 px (1440 × 2560 is sharper on large phones), quiet in the lower half where the copy sits on a phone (brief H1-M)." },
    { "type": "video", "id": "video", "label": "Film (optional)", "info": "8 to 12 seconds, silent, loops cleanly, same framing as the photograph (brief H1-F). Plays only on screen, never for reduced motion or Save-Data, always with a pause button." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "photo_alt", "label": "Photograph description", "info": "Used only if the image has no alt text in Content > Files." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "drawn_light", "label": "Drawn light and mist", "default": false, "info": "Adds drawn light shafts and a band of haze over the photograph. Leave off when the photograph has real light and fog of its own." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "rays_x", "label": "Light source across the photograph", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 2, "unit": "%", "default": 62 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "rays_x_mobile", "label": "Light source across the phone photograph", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 2, "unit": "%", "default": 34 },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Copy" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Perfume oil · Balm stick" },
    { "type": "inline_richtext", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Made for wherever you’re headed." },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "body", "label": "Body" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "note", "label": "Fine print", "info": "One short true line, or nothing." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta_label", "label": "Primary button", "default": "Shop Zorev" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "cta_link", "label": "Primary link" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta2_label", "label": "Secondary button", "info": "[pair_price] is replaced by the pair price from Theme settings > Offers." },
    { "type": "url", "id": "cta2_link", "label": "Secondary link" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Product card (wide screens)" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_card", "label": "Show the product card", "default": true },
    { "type": "product", "id": "product_a", "label": "First product", "info": "Empty: the pair from Theme settings > Offers." },
    { "type": "product", "id": "product_b", "label": "Second product" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "card_index_b", "label": "Second product: studio image", "min": 1, "max": 3, "step": 1, "default": 2, "info": "Which of the second product's studio images (Theme settings > Studio images) the card shows." },
    { "type": "url", "id": "card_link", "label": "Card link", "info": "Empty: the product line-up below (#line)." }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Cinematic hero" }]
}
{% endschema %}
